<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dahshur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dahshur is a royal necropolis on the west bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saqqara">Saqqara</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. The Fourth Dynasty king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sneferu">Sneferu</a> built two pyramids there in the 26th century BCE, the Bent Pyramid and the Red Pyramid, the first true smooth-sided pyramid. Kings of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-francia">Middle Kingdom</a> also built pyramids at Dahshur, and the burials of their royal women yielded fine jewellery.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dahshur.jpg" alt="Dahshur" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daniel Mayer · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dahshur_-_Red_Pyramid_-_Tourist_policemen_on_camel.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
